---
const steps = ["Plan", "Change", "Check", "Continue"];
---
<div class="walkthrough" data-tabset>
  <div class="workflow-tabs tab-controls" data-tablist aria-label="Task walkthrough" hidden>
    {steps.map((step, index) => <button type="button" id={`step-tab-${index}`} data-tab aria-controls={`step-panel-${index}`}>{step}</button>)}
  </div>
  <section id="step-panel-0" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><h3>Agree on what should happen.</h3><p>The test already showed the problem: names had extra spaces, and blank entries stayed in the list. The agent saved a plan for the fix.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">The next step was clear before the code changed.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record">
      <p class="record-label">The agreed change</p>
      <ul class="acceptance-list"><li>Trim surrounding whitespace.</li><li>Drop names that become empty.</li><li>Lowercase the remaining names.</li></ul>
      <div class="record-check"><span class="record-note">Run the existing test</span><code>python3 -m unittest -q</code><span>Keep the existing test unchanged.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-1" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><h3>Fix the cause.</h3><p>The function filtered names before trimming them. A string containing spaces counted as a name.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">The agent changed the function through Magistr and saved what it did.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record code-record">
      <p class="record-label">names.py</p>
      <div class="code-change"><span class="change-label">Before</span><pre><code>def normalize_names(names):
    return [name.lower() for name in names if name]</code></pre></div>
      <div class="code-change added"><span class="change-label">After</span><pre><code>def normalize_names(names):
    stripped_names = (name.strip() for name in names)
    return [name.lower() for name in stripped_names if name]</code></pre></div>
      <p class="record-foot">One source file changed. The test stayed the same.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-2" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><h3>Check that the fix works.</h3><p>The agent reproduced the failure, made the fix, then ran the same test through Magistr. The result was saved with the task.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">A later session can see which test ran and whether it passed.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record verification-record">
      <p class="record-label">Test result</p>
      <code class="check-command">python3 -m unittest -q</code>
      <div class="check-comparison"><div><span class="record-note">Before the fix</span><strong class="failed-result">Failed</strong><span>1 test · exit 1</span></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="record-note">After the fix</span><strong class="passed-result">Passed</strong><span>1 test · exit 0</span></div></div>
      <p class="record-foot">This result belongs to the recorded example. It is not a live test.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="step-panel-3" class="workflow-panel" data-panel>
    <div class="workflow-explanation"><h3>Come back in a fresh session.</h3><p>A fresh Codex session read the saved task. It could explain the bug, the fix, and the passing test without doing the work again.</p><p class="workflow-takeaway">It still needs to read the current code before starting the next change.</p></div>
    <div class="example-record resume-record">
      <p class="record-label">What the next session found</p>
      <dl><div><dt>Defect</dt><dd>Spaces survived; blank names stayed in the list.</dd></div><div><dt>Change</dt><dd>Trim once, drop empty names, then lowercase.</dd></div><div><dt>Check</dt><dd>One unchanged test passed. Exit code 0.</dd></div></dl>
      <a class="text-link" href="#evidence">Read the recorded sessions</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="walkthrough-foot"><span>From the contact-list sessions recorded on October 19.</span><a href="/docs/concepts#checking-your-work">What a passing check tells you</a></div>
</div>
<script>
  import "../scripts/tabs";
</script>